<h1>Terms &amp; FAQ</h1>

<dl class="faq">
  <dt>What is Dawn of the Devs?</dt>
  <dd>
    Dawn of the Devs is an IndieWeb webring &mdash; a collection of web developer portfolios linked together
    in a ring. Visitors can navigate from site to site using the "previous" and "next" links
    that each member adds to their page.
  </dd>

  <dt>Who can join?</dt>
  <dd>
    Anyone with a web developer portfolio! Your site should be something you own and control,
    not a profile on a social media platform. It should represent you and your work on the web.
  </dd>

  <dt>How do I join?</dt>
  <dd>
    <ol>
      <li>Add <strong>previous</strong> and <strong>next</strong> links to your site that point to
        <code><%= baseUrl %>/previous</code> and <code><%= baseUrl %>/next</code>.</li>
      <li>Sign in on the <a href="/">home page</a> using your domain via IndieAuth.</li>
      <li>Check your links from the dashboard to activate your membership.</li>
      <li>Optionally, add an <a href="https://indieweb.org/h-card">h-card</a> to your site
        so your profile appears in the <a href="/directory">directory</a>.</li>
    </ol>
  </dd>

  <dt>What is IndieAuth?</dt>
  <dd>
    <a href="https://indieauth.net/">IndieAuth</a> is a way to sign in using your own domain name.
    You set up your site to delegate authentication (e.g., via
    <a href="https://indielogin.com/">indielogin.com</a> or your own authorization endpoint),
    and you can sign in anywhere that supports it.
  </dd>

  <dt>What is an h-card?</dt>
  <dd>
    An <a href="https://indieweb.org/h-card">h-card</a> is a microformat for marking up your
    profile information (name, photo, bio) in HTML. If your site has an h-card, Dawn of the Devs
    will use it to show your profile in the directory.
  </dd>

  <dt>How does the ring navigation work?</dt>
  <dd>
    When someone clicks "next" or "previous" on a member's site, the webring looks at the
    <code>Referer</code> header to figure out which site they're coming from, then redirects
    to the next or previous member in the ring. If no referer is available, a random member is chosen.
  </dd>

  <dt>What happens if my site goes down?</dt>
  <dd>
    An automated gatekeeper periodically checks all member sites. If your site is unreachable or
    missing the required webring links, it will be marked inactive and removed from the ring
    rotation. Once your site is back and the links are in place, it will be re-activated on
    the next check.
  </dd>

  <dt>Can I remove my site?</dt>
  <dd>
    Yes. Sign in to your dashboard and remove the webring links from your site. The next
    gatekeeper check will mark your site as inactive. You can also remove your profile from
    the directory at any time from the dashboard.
  </dd>

  <dt>Is there a code of conduct?</dt>
  <dd>
    Be a decent human. Sites containing hate speech, harassment, illegal content, or malware
    will be removed. This is a community of people who build things for the web &mdash; let's
    keep it welcoming and positive.
  </dd>
</dl>

